--- body ---
## Context

Early `erg init` bundles (pre spec 0.1; e.g. AEDIST PR #570, 2026-05-25)
vendored five `.claude/skills/ticket-{new,claim,close,ready,release}/`
skills into host repos, plus a managed CLAUDE.md block claiming "no CLI
needed" and pointing the validator at `tickets/tools/go/`. Those skills
duplicated `erg <verb>` in prose and drifted: they described `%erg v1`
with a `Status:` header, which the 0.1 validator rejects.

The current source no longer ships any of this. But existing host
installs keep the orphans until someone hand-deletes them (AEDIST had
to: commit bbd2670d), and stale hook commands like
`tickets/tools/go/erg validate tickets/` linger in host
`.claude/settings.json` (AEDIST tickets/0526).

## Actions

All in `erg migrate` (the layout step, which already runs only when DIR is
the canonical `tickets/` and already removes tickets/tools/, content-rewrites
the pre-commit hook, and refreshes AGENTS.md — same vintage of cleanup):

1. Detect and remove previously-vendored `.claude/skills/ticket-*` dirs.
   Those bundles predate provenance markers, so match the known vendored
   content — tell-tale legacy substrings (`%erg v1`, `Status:` header
   prose) rather than exact hashes, since hosts may carry minor local
   edits. Only delete when the tell-tale content is present.
2. Rewrite/refresh the managed `# --- git-erg ---` CLAUDE.md block if
   present, dropping "no CLI needed" / `tickets/tools/go/` / `%erg v1`
   claims.
3. Comprehensive stale-reference sweep, not a hand-picked file list:
   walk the ENTIRE work tree — a plain filesystem walk, not git
   ls-files, because hook-definition files like
   `.claude/settings.local.json` are routinely gitignored and are
   exactly what this sweep exists for — plus the repository hooks dir,
   for the legacy patterns `tickets/tools/go/erg` -> `tickets/erg` and
   `erg validate tickets/` -> `erg check tickets/`, and rewrite them
   content-based and idempotently wherever they appear — git hooks,
   `.claude/settings.json`, GitHub workflows (.github/workflows/),
   other forge CI (.gitlab-ci.yml, .woodpecker/, Jenkinsfile, ...),
   Makefiles, scripts. Skip binary files, files over 2 MiB (wiring is
   hand-written and small), and the ticket store itself
   (ticket text may legitimately quote old paths as history). This
   generalises the pre-commit-only migrateHook; AEDIST tickets/0526
   found the same rot in .claude/settings.json, and CI configs and
   Make rules are the same class of host-side reference.
4. Emit a one-line notice for each artifact pruned and each file
   rewritten by the sweep (path + which pattern).
5. Optionally, `erg update` may *detect* the orphans post-swap and print
   "run erg migrate" guidance (parallel to its Status:-header hint), but
   it never mutates them itself.

## Test

First (red) test: install the old bundle into a scratch repo with stale
references seeded across the sweep surface — skills present, stale
CLAUDE.md block, `.claude/settings.json` hook, a `.github/workflows/`
job, a Makefile rule, and `.git/hooks/pre-commit`, all referencing
`tickets/tools/go/erg ... validate tickets/`. Run `erg migrate tickets`,
assert the `.claude/skills/ticket-*` directories are gone, the managed
block no longer mentions skills or `%erg v1`, and every seeded file now
reads `tickets/erg ... check tickets/`. Also seed a ticket body quoting
the old path and a file with no legacy pattern: both must be untouched.

## Invariants

- `erg migrate` never touches skills or CLAUDE.md content outside the
  git-erg managed blocks / known vendored content (skill dirs without
  the tell-tale legacy content are left alone).
- The sweep rewrites only exact legacy patterns; files without a match
  are byte-identical afterwards. Ticket store and binary files exempt.
- Re-running `erg migrate` is idempotent.
- `erg update` keeps its binary-only contract: it may hint, never prune.
- Like the rest of migrate: never commits; user reviews the diff.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `erg migrate` removes previously-installed `ticket-*` skills from a
      host repo (verified on a scratch install of the old bundle).
- [x] The managed CLAUDE.md block, when refreshed, references
      `erg <verb>` and `%erg 0.1`, with no "no CLI needed" /
      `tickets/tools/go/` claims.
- [x] The repo-wide sweep rewrites stale `tickets/tools/go/erg` /
      `validate tickets/` references wherever they occur (git hooks,
      .claude/settings.json and gitignored settings.local.json, CI
      workflows, Makefiles, scripts), and leaves non-matching files and
      the ticket store byte-identical.
- [x] Scratch-repo migrate test passes and is idempotent.
